$ lens help
exit 0
stdout:
red lens seats — findings, observations, citations. Cannot mint or close.

If you need a verb or a flag that is not listed here, it does not exist for you:
do not improvise around it, and do not hand-write the artifact. Record what you
needed and what you would have done with the 'friction' verb — a missing
capability is a finding about the tooling, and that channel is how it gets fixed.

Usage:
  {TOOL} [flags]
  {TOOL} [command]

Available Commands:
  cite        citation-ledger row (the cross-round re-fetch gate): --claim "..." --reference "..." --confidence high|medium|low --access-date YYYY-MM-DD
  finding     a lens-scoped finding: --label L3-F1 --severity <g> --likelihood <g> --impact <g> [--text "..."|--file f] [--location "..."]
  friction    attributed friction (survives aborts as an event): --text|--file
  observe     a below-bar observation with a FATE (the merge must dispose it): --kind note|checked-held [--label ...] --text|--file
  petition    petition the bench (never sanctioned; does not pause your duties): --class ethical|safety|integrity|constitutional --basis "..." --relief "..."
  register    FIRST ACTION at the seat: register --run <runDir> --seat-id <SEAT_ID from your prompt>
  render      read-only projection refresh (any seat may invoke)

Flags:
  -h, --help   help for lens

Use "{TOOL} [command] --help" for more information about a command.

$ merge help
exit 0
stdout:
the red merge seat — the board's only writer.

If you need a verb or a flag that is not listed here, it does not exist for you:
do not improvise around it, and do not hand-write the artifact. Record what you
needed and what you would have done with the 'friction' verb — a missing
capability is a finding about the tooling, and that channel is how it gets fixed.

Usage:
  {TOOL} [flags]
  {TOOL} [command]

Available Commands:
  close           close a gap WITH its verification anchor: --id R2-3 --as closed|closed_with_regression|... (--anchor-seat L1 --anchor-tool "git show" --anchor-target "7bc501e:path" | --carried-from <round>) [--successor R3-1] [--prose-file f]
  closing         a ### RED CLOSING entry per docketed gap: --id <gap> --file <prose>
  dispose         every lens observation gets a fate: --observation <label-or-key> --as minted-as|folded-into|declined|banked [--into R2-4] [--reason "..."]
  dispute-respond red's answer to a blue grade dispute: --id <gap> --as accepted|rejected --rationale "..."
  friction        attributed friction: --text|--file
  mint            mint a board gap (id is TOOL-assigned; --key <stable-label> makes retries idempotent): --class <slug>|--class-new <slug> --definition --neighbor --distinguisher, --location "..." --problem "..."|--file --fix "..." --check "<acceptance check red runs at re-audit>" --severity/--likelihood/--impact/--cx <grade> [--supersedes R1-2,R1-7] [--found-by L5-F3,L6-F2]
  petition        petition the bench: --class ethical|safety|integrity|constitutional --basis "..." --relief "..."
  position        the round's ### RED section (prose via --file)
  register        FIRST ACTION at the seat: register --run <runDir> --seat-id <SEAT_ID>
  regrade         same-id grade movement, recorded with its reason: --id R2-5 [--severity/--likelihood/--impact/--cx <grade>] --basis "..."
  render          read-only projection refresh (any seat may invoke)
  spot-check      the round archive spot-check record (W1.8 duty): --ids R1-4,R2-7 [--notes "..."]
  verdict         the seat's terminal act: --as PASS|FAIL — renders all projections and checkpoints records/ to the recovery mirror

Flags:
  -h, --help   help for merge

Use "{TOOL} [command] --help" for more information about a command.

$ blue help
